--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY (web -> native)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web leaf is a presentational component: a `GlassPanel` with a `Settings` (gear) header + the
"Vehicle Configuration" title, and a 12-row `KVList columns={2}`; when `vehicleConfig` is null it renders a
`Skeleton`. Props: `vehicleConfig: VehicleConfigSnapshot | null | undefined`, `softwareVersion: string |
undefined`. The native surface reproduces its data, composition, states, and i18n keys, widening the web's
content-vs-skeleton branch to the full P4 load envelope its parent vehicle-detail page owns.

- Data sources bound via the shared state-holder seam (P1/S8); no HTTP in the view:
    useTranslation -> VCSectionStrings (P1/S10 NSLocalizedString facade, table "VehicleConfigSection").
  The whole `vehicleConfig`/`softwareVersion`/isLoading/error/freshness lifecycle is delivered by a
  `VehicleConfigSectionSource` (P1/S8); the view binds `VehicleConfigSectionModel` and never networks.

- web `configItems` ternaries ported 1:1 (VehicleConfigSection.Adapter.swift, dependency-free):
    • string fields  -> `field ?? '—'`              (car_type, trim, exterior_color, wheel_type,
                                                       roof_color, charge_port, rear_seat_heaters,
                                                       sunroof_installed)
    • boolean fields -> `flag != null ? (Yes : No) : '—'`  (right_hand_drive, europe_vehicle,
                                                             offroad_lightbar_present)
    • software       -> `software_update_version ?? softwareVersion ?? '—'`
  The 12 rows are emitted in the EXACT web source order (VCSectionField.ordered), pinned by a test.

- Shared components mapped (atomic shared components are out of scope per the prompt — REUSED, not
  redefined): @/components/ui GlassPanel -> TSGlassPanel; the web `KVList columns={2}` -> a responsive
  two-column LazyVGrid of label/value rows (one column on compact width) reusing the shared tokens, with a
  hairline divider per row (web `divide-y`); @/components/feedback Skeleton -> TSSkeleton (loading) and
  EmptyState -> ContentUnavailableView (empty). The page-level web `FadeIn` -> TSFadeIn.

- i18n keys present in P1/S10 table (.strings) — parity keys EXACTLY from source (15):
    vehicles.detail.vehicleConfig / carType / trim / color / wheels / roofColor / chargePort / rhd /
    europeVehicle / offroadLightbar / rearSeatHeaters / sunroofInstalled / softwareVersion,
    common.yes / common.no  (+ native chrome under configSection.* and the empty sentence
    vehicles.detail.noVehicleConfig). No English string literals in Swift — every label resolves through
    the facade; values come from the snapshot.

- States rendered (no hidden surface): loading (2-col skeleton rows), empty (web EmptyState ->
  ContentUnavailableView, gear glyph + sentence — never a blank box), error (web QueryError equivalent
  with a Retry affordance), content (responsive 1-col compact / 2-col regular KV grid, web
  `KVList columns={2}`); connection axis live/stale/offline (freshness chip + cached-data banner + one-shot
  auto-refresh on the stale transition; offline keeps the cached rows and does not refetch).

- Accessibility: per-row combined labels (label + value), decorative icons hidden, panel-level VoiceOver
  summary (title + each label/value); Dynamic Type via tokens; Reduce-Motion respected by TSFadeIn /
  TSSkeleton.

- Telemetry: view.opened emitted once on start() with surface slug "VehicleConfigSection" (P1/S11).

- Module-collision avoidance (parallel-merge safety): the surface uses the `VCSection*` prefix throughout.
  Verified app-wide UNIQUE: `struct VehicleConfigSection` defined exactly 1x (this file); 0 other files
  define any `VCSection*` symbol.

